WEBVTT

00:08.370 --> 00:15.570
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.370 --> 00:15.570
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.610 --> 00:22.320
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.610 --> 00:22.320
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.120 --> 00:30.920
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.120 --> 00:30.920
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:30.960 --> 00:35.630
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:30.960 --> 00:35.630
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.230 --> 00:44.630
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.230 --> 00:44.630
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.680 --> 00:52.310
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.680 --> 00:52.310
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.390 --> 01:01.590
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.390 --> 01:01.590
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.590 --> 01:08.730
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.590 --> 01:08.730
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:08.900 --> 01:16.030
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:08.900 --> 01:16.030
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.140 --> 01:23.640
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.140 --> 01:23.640
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:35.860 --> 01:38.690
I thought that it'd rained quite a bit
this summer, but...

01:39.060 --> 01:40.700
A water shortage?

01:40.700 --> 01:41.390
Yeah...

01:41.460 --> 01:42.230


01:42.230 --> 01:45.730
I guess it doesn't matter if it rains
at a seaside town like ours.

01:45.730 --> 01:47.770
The flower shops must be having a hard time.

01:48.540 --> 01:51.510
And your flower arranging too, right?

01:51.510 --> 01:55.080
Well it's more like a hobby for me.

01:55.080 --> 01:56.370
That's not true, and you know it.

01:56.680 --> 01:57.840
Thank you for the food.

01:58.850 --> 01:59.540
You've had enough?

02:00.520 --> 02:01.240
Yes.

02:03.090 --> 02:05.550
I need to finish the wreath.

02:05.550 --> 02:07.550
I'm bringing with me when
I go back to school tomorrow.

02:24.210 --> 02:25.340
Manatsu.

02:25.340 --> 02:25.860
Yes?

02:28.010 --> 02:32.210
Manatsu, please take care of Ichika.

02:32.210 --> 02:34.180
Hey, what's with that all of a sudden?

02:34.180 --> 02:35.340
This is new...

02:38.390 --> 02:42.520
We do not know exactly what you are.

02:43.290 --> 02:49.460
But for her this is the last summer
she will spend here.

02:49.970 --> 02:53.600
We leave her in your hands during this time.

02:56.270 --> 02:57.400
Don't worry.

02:58.910 --> 03:02.240
I love Ichika.

03:02.240 --> 03:05.210
Since long, long ago.

03:07.950 --> 03:11.250
No matter what happens, I will never betray her.

03:12.690 --> 03:15.020
Hearing those words gladdens our hearts.

03:18.090 --> 03:19.220
Thank you.

03:22.300 --> 03:26.800
The Flush of Damp Skin

03:35.040 --> 03:35.640
Ouch!

03:44.020 --> 03:45.920
Are you okay, Ichika?

03:45.920 --> 03:47.120
Manatsu...

03:48.590 --> 03:51.690
You're really pretty clumsy, Ichika.

03:51.690 --> 03:53.060
Where were those band aids again?

03:53.060 --> 03:55.200
Band aids, band aids...

03:55.200 --> 03:57.220
Um, were they here?

03:58.230 --> 03:59.030
Huh?

03:59.500 --> 04:00.970
Ichika, what's with this?

04:01.970 --> 04:04.560
I want to stop.

04:05.210 --> 04:06.470
I want to stop using it.

04:07.910 --> 04:12.780
I want to stop using... the power of the Djinn.

04:15.280 --> 04:19.550
It was your homework
to start with, right Manatsu?

04:20.160 --> 04:22.120
Sure, you can stop.

04:23.490 --> 04:25.020
Really?

04:25.690 --> 04:26.680
But in return,

04:30.530 --> 04:35.030
this charm won't return to normal,
and I can't give it back to you.

04:37.140 --> 04:38.270
Are you okay with that?

04:40.040 --> 04:42.140
Why don't I give it to you, Ichika?

04:44.110 --> 04:45.880
Thank you very much!

04:45.880 --> 04:48.080
I'll treasure it, I promise!

05:05.700 --> 05:07.370
I'm sorry...

05:07.370 --> 05:09.390
I just can't...

05:11.410 --> 05:14.310
The charm in which resides
the power of the Djinn

05:14.310 --> 05:17.910
was originally something I received from Sei.

05:17.910 --> 05:23.010
I just couldn't bear myself to throw it away.

05:45.010 --> 05:46.370
It's a dream...

05:46.780 --> 05:48.770
I'm having that dream again.

05:49.210 --> 05:51.940
I've had this dream how many times before?

05:52.780 --> 05:57.450
But each time I awaken,
I can never remember it...

05:58.350 --> 06:00.090
Manatsu...

06:00.090 --> 06:03.520
I am you, and you are me...

06:03.530 --> 06:05.330
I'm sorry, Ichika.

06:05.330 --> 06:08.260
But I'm going to...

06:11.400 --> 06:12.990
...kill you.

06:44.130 --> 06:48.190
I feel like I was dreaming, but...

06:55.780 --> 06:58.750
Oh, what am I going to do with you, Manatsu?

07:20.270 --> 07:22.040
Good mornin'...

07:22.040 --> 07:24.230
Where's Ichika?

07:24.640 --> 07:26.270
Good morning, Manatsu.

07:26.640 --> 07:29.440
Today Ichika has to go to the school.

07:29.440 --> 07:32.140
She said they were going to the hospital
as volunteers to visit the sick.

07:35.650 --> 07:37.550
I guess it'll be okay.

07:37.890 --> 07:40.220
Even though Ichika seemed so upset by it...

07:49.160 --> 07:51.200
Good morning, Ichika!

07:51.200 --> 07:51.960
Good morning!

07:52.270 --> 07:53.970
A good morning to you.

07:53.970 --> 07:55.490
Good morning.

07:56.100 --> 07:58.640
The construction is really coming along.

07:58.640 --> 08:03.140
Sheesh, what was the point of us
cleaning it up like that?

08:03.180 --> 08:04.710
Yes.

08:04.710 --> 08:08.380
But so much for one of the seven mysteries.

08:13.090 --> 08:15.250
The large mirror, one of the seven legends...

08:16.090 --> 08:19.030
Where I met first Manatsu.

08:21.100 --> 08:23.290
Hurry up already, we're going to be late!

08:24.200 --> 08:25.760
Roger!

08:41.350 --> 08:44.590
I haven't heard from Nozomu...

08:44.590 --> 08:45.880
Not even email?

08:46.990 --> 08:48.890
It has been a while.

08:50.060 --> 08:52.060
Manatsu isn't here.

08:52.060 --> 08:54.530
Ah, you're right.

08:54.530 --> 08:55.760
But...

08:55.760 --> 08:56.360
But?

08:57.700 --> 09:01.260
It was always like this before summer break.

09:01.970 --> 09:03.630
Things have changed.

09:06.540 --> 09:09.740
The building up ahead
is the rehabilitation center.

09:09.740 --> 09:12.740
It's a place that doesn't just heal the body,
but the spirit as well.

09:13.180 --> 09:17.050
So please hang up your wreaths and
help to heal people's hearts.

09:17.490 --> 09:19.390
Here, go ahead.

09:19.690 --> 09:20.880
Next.

09:21.720 --> 09:23.790
That'll be fine, good.

09:23.790 --> 09:25.260
Next.

09:33.400 --> 09:34.600
It's wonderful.

09:34.600 --> 09:36.840
All set.

09:36.840 --> 09:38.470
Thank you very much!

09:53.190 --> 09:56.760
I'm glad they liked your wreath, Michiru.

09:56.760 --> 09:57.660
Yes.

09:57.660 --> 09:59.750
The room I'm supposed to go to is...

10:07.600 --> 10:07.640
This is it, yes?

10:07.640 --> 10:09.440
This is it, yes?

10:09.440 --> 10:11.070
But I'm hungry!

10:11.070 --> 10:11.100


10:12.270 --> 10:13.640
I can't do that.

10:13.640 --> 10:16.270
You need to manage on three meals a day.

10:16.710 --> 10:17.880
Jerk.

10:17.880 --> 10:19.950
Call me a jerk if you'd like.

10:19.950 --> 10:23.250
I am simply worried about your health,
Ms. Shirasaka.

10:23.250 --> 10:27.090
Is Shirasaka even my real name?

10:27.090 --> 10:28.490
Yes, it is.

10:28.490 --> 10:31.550
Oh, you must be the volunteer students.

10:32.360 --> 10:33.260
Yes.

10:37.870 --> 10:38.660
Okay.

10:38.970 --> 10:42.640
Ms. Shirasaka, they brought you
your favorite, flowers!

10:42.640 --> 10:43.540
Flowers?

10:44.670 --> 10:49.170
Anyway, overeating will stress your body,
and this will all be for nothing.

10:49.780 --> 10:52.650
Take your time, and regain your memories.

10:52.650 --> 10:54.820
Thank you so much every day.

10:54.820 --> 10:59.290
These volunteers have brought
a wreath they made.

10:59.290 --> 10:59.980
If you'll excuse me.

11:02.060 --> 11:04.160
You like flowers?

11:04.160 --> 11:06.490
Show me... Hurry and show me!

11:06.490 --> 11:07.760
Uh, sure...

11:07.760 --> 11:10.090
If you'd like, we'll hang it up in your room.

11:11.430 --> 11:12.730
Flowers!

11:22.640 --> 11:23.630
No...

11:24.410 --> 11:25.640
No...

11:26.180 --> 11:28.550
Where are the flowers?

11:29.650 --> 11:32.750
Well, those are dried flowers, so...

11:32.750 --> 11:33.850
No!

11:34.690 --> 11:38.020
These... These aren't flowers!

11:38.790 --> 11:42.730
These are... These are...
These are... These are...

11:43.030 --> 11:45.370
Wrong... Wrong... Wrong!

11:45.370 --> 11:48.200
This pile of garbage isn't flowers!

11:49.800 --> 11:51.170
Garbage?

11:53.880 --> 11:54.840
Garbage?!

11:58.480 --> 12:01.570
Mother, can I have these flowers?

12:01.920 --> 12:04.280
Sure. What are you going to do with them?

12:05.020 --> 12:06.920
It's for the volunteer work this summer.

12:06.920 --> 12:09.090
Oh, you're going to dry them.

12:09.090 --> 12:09.920
Go on ahead.

12:16.230 --> 12:17.260
Those are lovely.

12:19.730 --> 12:20.760
Thank you...

12:22.140 --> 12:24.500
They aren't garbage...

12:25.170 --> 12:27.440
These are dead, dried flowers!

12:27.440 --> 12:29.600
I don't want to look at garbage like this!

12:30.280 --> 12:33.840
I want to die, surrounded by living flowers...

12:37.390 --> 12:39.320
They aren't garbage.

12:44.660 --> 12:47.030
No, Ichika!

12:47.030 --> 12:48.830
You mustn't!

12:56.840 --> 12:57.830
Ichika...

13:16.290 --> 13:17.280
In that case...

13:17.760 --> 13:23.760
What? I don't want to use
the Djinn's power anymore...

13:24.330 --> 13:29.130
In that case I'll wrap you
in the flowers you desire.

13:30.610 --> 13:33.580
What am I saying?

14:16.250 --> 14:17.240
Ichika...

14:37.870 --> 14:39.140
What's going on?

14:45.450 --> 14:46.850
Flowers...

14:46.850 --> 14:48.580
There are so many flowers!

14:52.720 --> 14:54.120
I'm so happy...

15:10.370 --> 15:12.240
What's happening?

15:37.870 --> 15:39.100
Oh, no!

15:39.100 --> 15:41.570
Please, somebody help!

15:42.670 --> 15:45.210
I called a nurse.

15:45.210 --> 15:46.610
Pardon me!

15:46.610 --> 15:47.870
Ms. Shirasaka?

15:47.880 --> 15:50.940
Ms. Shirasaka, are you all right?

15:50.950 --> 15:52.050
Ms. Shirasaka!

15:52.050 --> 15:53.670
Did something happen?

15:54.320 --> 15:55.520
I don't know.

15:55.520 --> 15:56.640
She just suddenly...

15:57.020 --> 15:58.110
Oh, no!

16:00.350 --> 16:03.050
Shiho, where are you?

16:04.160 --> 16:06.060
Is Shiho here?

16:06.730 --> 16:07.750
Mitsuki...

16:08.200 --> 16:09.530
Her memories?

16:10.730 --> 16:11.660
Shiho?

16:12.170 --> 16:13.190
Mitsuki!

16:16.400 --> 16:19.000
Mitsuki, you know who I am?

16:19.410 --> 16:24.570
Shiho, I was surrounded by flowers... Flowers!

16:24.880 --> 16:26.010
How's the ICU?

16:26.010 --> 16:27.210
#3 is open.

16:27.220 --> 16:29.080
Hurry! Are you all set?

16:29.080 --> 16:30.150
All set!

16:30.150 --> 16:32.450
Ready, set... go!

16:34.990 --> 16:36.420
Anaphylaxis...

16:37.020 --> 16:39.530
That's what they call an acute allergic reaction.

16:39.530 --> 16:41.790
Like a serious allergy to pollen.

16:42.560 --> 16:47.900
The two of us ran a flower shop,
but she suddenly developed that illness.

16:49.600 --> 16:52.770
She really loves flowers,

16:53.410 --> 16:56.900
so when she couldn't continue running the shop,
she was devastated.

16:57.850 --> 17:00.710
She tried to kill herself again and again.

17:04.350 --> 17:07.890
And in the process she lost her memories.

17:07.890 --> 17:12.390
She forgot everything, even me, her little sister.

17:12.660 --> 17:14.750
But did you see her face?

17:15.400 --> 17:16.730
She was glad.

17:17.030 --> 17:22.440
Shiho, I was surrounded by flowers... Flowers!

17:24.610 --> 17:28.560
Maybe the flower spirit let her see an illusion.

17:29.810 --> 17:33.710
She called out my name, "Shiho".

17:33.710 --> 17:37.310
She remembered me...

17:55.370 --> 17:59.860
Will I never live with flowers again?

18:00.510 --> 18:03.940
There are many excellent
artificial flowers today, you know.

18:06.480 --> 18:10.110
I wonder if she'll try again?

18:23.970 --> 18:27.560
I don't want to go home.

18:37.450 --> 18:38.500
No way!

18:39.550 --> 18:40.710
It's gone!

18:42.020 --> 18:48.320
The mirror that Manatsu came out of... it's gone!

18:59.530 --> 19:00.590
My eyes...

19:06.240 --> 19:08.680
It's not Manatsu's fault...

19:08.680 --> 19:10.640
It's not Manatsu's fault...

19:31.770 --> 19:35.900
I'm... a bad girl...

19:45.380 --> 19:46.710
Ichika...

20:05.730 --> 20:08.040
Are you okay, Ichika?

20:08.040 --> 20:08.560
Stay away!

20:10.470 --> 20:12.270
I'm sorry...

20:12.810 --> 20:15.540
I'm not clean right now...

20:24.320 --> 20:29.150
Ichika, I know this must be
a difficult time for you,

20:29.720 --> 20:32.660
but you mustn't let the pressure get to you.

20:33.460 --> 20:38.400
All I can do is watch over you, but good luck.

20:38.800 --> 20:39.960
Sei...

20:42.870 --> 20:47.370
At that time I no longer knew
what to believe in any more.

20:49.310 --> 20:53.840
And above all else,
I lost the confidence in myself.

20:59.620 --> 21:02.190
Were you the one who sent this?

21:02.190 --> 21:03.120
My bad.

21:03.860 --> 21:07.060
Isn't it a violation of the rules?

21:07.730 --> 21:13.030
I'm happy to take the penalty,
the punishment, all by myself...

21:16.070 --> 21:17.000
Kai...

21:40.730 --> 21:42.290
It's almost time.

21:47.500 --> 21:50.470


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.400 --> 23:20.500


23:20.500 --> 23:21.500


23:21.500 --> 23:24.300
The heart that resides in the flesh
known as the body

23:24.300 --> 23:26.630
should be able to manipulate it.

23:26.630 --> 23:30.000
On that day I came to realize
that there is something else

23:30.000 --> 23:32.740
that envelopes the heart and, before you know it,

23:32.740 --> 23:34.440
comes to manipulate it.

23:34.810 --> 23:39.810
On the next Uta~Kata:
The Pain of Love
